Original commit body from e696e546807f4aba5e3eafbf68c0b4cf2e1e54d4:

`property` sat in the blanket noise set labelled "CSS structural". No CSS
analyzer has ever emitted it: css.py and scss.py had no kind="property" when
the entry was added (4eab1afde7) and have none now. Its real producers are
five analyzers, and they mean different things by it:
- swift: a computed property, a callable with a body;
- C#: a property with get/set bodies;
- .properties: a config key;
- QML: a property declaration;
- objective-c: a bodyless @property.

MEASURED, analyzer level (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tisom_09242026/):
- swift, 5 repos: 3,323 property symbols, 12,552 call edges out, 364 in.
- objective-c (4 repos), QML (1) and .properties (3): 91,695 property
  symbols, 0 edges either way. They stay noise.
- C#, 4 repos: 201 property symbols, 1 edge in, 0 out. A fixture shows why:
  the analyzer emits no edge for a call inside an accessor (filed WI-binap).
  C# properties become visible, but they carry no call edges until that is fixed.
The row named rst as a producer. It is not: API_DIRECTIVES is a name set, and
rst emits kind="directive".

MEASURED, default survey, node and edge sets, dev 9f2e8f06d7 vs this commit.
Nothing was removed; every added edge has a property endpoint:
- Alamofire: +346 property nodes, +279 edges (278 calls, 1 reference).
- Kingfisher: +282 property nodes, +681 edges (680 calls, 1 reference).
- sherpa-onnx: +225 property nodes (146 C#, 79 swift), +175 swift edges.
dead-code-maybe: Alamofire unchanged; Kingfisher 264 -> 262. The two leaving
(getAssociatedObject, setRetainedAssociatedObject) are called only from
computed-property getters.

WI-fadab (compact's default path never applies is_excluded_kind) is not
affected: `property` is not in EXCLUDED_KINDS.

A new gate, test_every_property_producer_is_classified, requires every
language-package module that emits kind="property" to be classified as noise
or not, so a sixth producer cannot inherit the drop silently.

